  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia has $3B in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Obligations are down 97.6% year over year. Award activity shows 19,644 awards with an average award size of $155K. Historical annual obligations illustrate the scale change: FY22 totaled $91.7B, FY23 totaled $109B, FY24 totaled $113B, FY25 totaled $124B, and FY26 totaled $126B. Buying patterns for FY2027 to date concentrate with the Department of Veterans Affairs at $1.5B, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $313M and the Department of Homeland Security at $313M. Vendor concentration for FY2027 to date shows TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $900M and ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $308M. Industry concentration for FY2027 to date is led by Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $900M and Computer Systems Design Services at $735M. This snapshot is a fiscal year to date view of obligation totals, award counts, buyer and vendor concentration, and top industries in Virginia.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which federal agencies are the biggest buyers in Virginia for FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $1.5B in obligations. The Department of Health and Human Services and the Department of Homeland Security each obligated $313M. The General Services Administration obligated $231M and the Department of Justice obligated $176M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal contractors and which industries receive the most obligations in Virginia for FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the top contractor with $900M in obligations, followed by ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $308M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $174M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers lead industries with $900M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services with $735M and Other Computer Related Services with $362M."
      }
    ]
  },
